Measurement data (inside the worker code's package, and in the files the apps ship)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Head-related impulse responses of the Neumann KU100 dummy head: src/pixl_worker/spatial/data/hrir_ku100.npz,
  derived from the SADIE II Database, subject D1 (D1_48K_24bit_256tap_FIR_SOFA.sofa in D1_HRIR_SOFA.zip), by
  AudioLab and Gavin Kearney, University of York.
  Licence: Apache-2.0  Text: LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt, and the licence's own notice for this data in
  LICENSES/SADIE-II.txt
  Source: https://zenodo.org/records/12092466 (version 2-2, doi:10.5281/zenodo.12092466)
  This file is not the original. tools/build_hrir.py made it from the database (2026-11-10): about 900 of the
  8802 measured directions are kept, the right half of the sphere is replaced by the mirror image of the left,
  the common leading silence is removed and the tails are faded out, the set is diffuse-field equalised, and the
  samples are stored as 16-bit integers with a scale factor.
  The on-device tables schema/v1/spatial/spatial_preview_v1.json and spatial_preview_golden_v1.json (shipped in
  both PixlAudio apps) are computed from that file by src/pixl_worker/spatial/preview.py, and every spatial
  render the worker produces is made with it.

