Base image and system packages
------------------------------
- pytorch/pytorch:2.11.0-cuda12.8-cudnn9-runtime (pinned by digest in the Dockerfile): PyTorch is BSD-3-Clause;
  the CUDA and cuDNN runtime libraries are under NVIDIA's redistributable-runtime terms, whose texts ship with
  them inside the base image; Ubuntu 24.04 packages keep their copyright files in /usr/share/doc/*/copyright.
- ffmpeg from Ubuntu 24.04 (apt). Ubuntu builds it with GPL components enabled, so the binaries are under the
  GPL: LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt, LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt and LICENSES/LGPL-2.1.txt, with the exact terms in
  /usr/share/doc/ffmpeg/copyright and /usr/share/doc/libavcodec*/copyright.
  Source: the Ubuntu source packages of the versions listed in /opt/pixl/apt-versions.txt (written at build
  time by dpkg-query), available from https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/ffmpeg and the Ubuntu archive.

Not included on purpose
-----------------------
No BS-RoFormer "SW" (6-stem) model (unknown licence and provenance) and no CC-BY-NC weights (MMS, the
ctc-forced-aligner default model, becruily deux).
